@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3100
@passcode = replace-with-local-passcode
@recordId = replace-with-record-uuid

# VS Code REST Client keeps the Set-Cookie from the login request in its cookie
# jar for this host. Run "Login" once, then the authenticated requests below.
# For curl, use: curl -c jar.txt -b jar.txt ...

### Health (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Login (sets mj_session HttpOnly cookie; body is empty)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "passcode": "{{passcode}}"
}

### 401 example: no cookie
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/records

### List records (default limit 50, max 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/records?limit=50

### List records with a cursor from the previous response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/records?limit=50&cursor=replace-with-next-cursor

### Create a record (date defaults to Asia/Hong_Kong today)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/records
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-21",
  "players": [
    { "name": "閒1", "score": 12.5 },
    { "name": "閒2", "score": -12.5 },
    { "name": "閒3", "score": 0 },
    { "name": "我", "score": 0 }
  ]
}

### Patch a record (date and/or players; players replaces the settlement set)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/records/{{recordId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-22",
  "players": [
    { "playerId": "replace-with-player-uuid", "name": "閒1", "score": 20 },
    { "playerId": "replace-with-player-uuid", "name": "閒2", "score": -20 }
  ]
}

### Delete a record (cascades settlements)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/records/{{recordId}}

### Players (for datalist)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/players

### Stats (year defaults to the current Hong Kong year)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stats?player=閒1&year=2026

### Ranking (all-time, full dataset)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ranking

### Logout (clears the cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
